        "id": 85130,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-28T04:50:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If my memory serves me correctly, I currently have 5 games against&nbsp;SkinWeaver and 3 against G-Spite. All of which have been victories.</p><p>Of those 5 games against SkinWeaver, 2 were DW versus him, both of which ended because NightMist was in Mist Form and allowed GloomWeaver to murder himself. 2 of the other games were randomized and happened to have Visionary in it, both of which ending thanks to Visionary in her Telekinetic Cocoon. The other game took play in&nbsp;Insula Primalis,&nbsp;Legacy with Next Evolution and Lead from the Front in play, making GloomWeaver's start of turn damage meaningless to the heroes, while Ra had Flesh of the Sun God handy, making the Volcanic Eruption meaningless to the heroes as well. One of these days the randomizer will give me heroes against GloomWeaver that won't be the heroes exploiting his self damaging tendency to self murder. However he is much more difficult then base GloomWeaver, because most of those games would of been loses.</p><p>Against G-Spite, 2 of them we decided to have him flip. One of those games were very entertaining, because we would abuse a Innocent Bystander like crazy, by saving him and releasing him 2 times a round. Fairly certain he was fed up with us, but he eventually died, so no witnesses to tell the tale. Overall I think his difficulty is about the same as base Spite, but he certainly is a lot more enjoyable of a game!</p>",
        "post_number": 72,
