        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-28T06:23:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Envisioner, I was at first going to reply to this in terms of actual philosophical argument, because there are so many fallacies and moral absolutist pollution floating around your arguments that it really bears dissection. &nbsp;But, for whatever reason, you seem to be completely unable to admit that you might just possibly be wrong, so I'm not going to waste my typing here.</p><p>But in the end? &nbsp;You're not a martyr here. &nbsp;You're not Martin Luther to whom you allude a comparison. &nbsp;You're not Ghandi. &nbsp;You're not doing anyone a service with your negativity and general argumentativeness. &nbsp;There's no tyranny here that you're fighting against, no injustice that's going to be righted by your adherence to a byzantine and illogical personal code.</p><p>You're arguing against the fundamental logic of mathematics on a&nbsp;<em>forum for a card game</em>. &nbsp; Honestly, man? &nbsp;<strong>Just.&nbsp;</strong><strong>Chill. Out.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
